[video here](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/e32c6df0-2df9-41da-ac0d-3e62d3ddf4ff)

Addresses race condition in tooltip setup where the dynamic import of Bootstrap's Tooltip class wasn't being properly awaited before creating instances. If categories changed during import, tooltips could be initialized for stale elements.

## Changes

- Moved `Tooltip` class declaration inside async function scope, ensuring it's only available after import completes
- Removed outer scope `let Tooltip: any` declaration that allowed unsafe access before import resolution

**Before:**
```typescript
let Tooltip: any;

const setupTooltips = async () => {
  Tooltip = (await import("bootstrap/js/dist/tooltip")).default;
  // Tooltip instances created here, but categories could change before import
  tooltipRefs.current.forEach((el, idx) => {
    if (el) tooltipInstances.current.push(new Tooltip(el));
  });
};

setupTooltips(); // Not awaited
```

**After:**
```typescript
const setupTooltips = async () => {
  const Tooltip = (await import("bootstrap/js/dist/tooltip")).default;
  // All setup logic executes after import completes
  tooltipRefs.current.forEach((el, idx) => {
    if (el) tooltipInstances.current.push(new Tooltip(el));
  });
};

setupTooltips();
```

This ensures tooltip creation is synchronous with respect to the current categories state after import resolution.

